To find the height of the pile formed by the three pipes in Crate B, let's start by analyzing the structure more closely. We know that there are three pipes arranged such that their centers form an equilateral triangle. Let’s denote the vertices of this equilateral triangle as \( A \), \( B \), and \( C \). These vertices represent the points where the pipes touch each other. Since the diameter of each pipe is \( 10 \) cm, the side length of the equilateral triangle formed by the centers of the pipes is also \( 10 \) cm.

[asy]
draw(circle((10,10),10),black+linewidth(1));
draw(circle((30,10),10),black+linewidth(1));
